# S10.2D-R7 rollback public-health gap — 2026-09-08

Status: `P0_PUBLIC_SFW_OUTAGE_FAIL_CLOSED_RECOVERY_AUTHORIZED`

## Observed state

- The single versioned R7 rollback restored Application source commit
  `f9747088a31ec6c671e82de24e293ebdec99f717`, tree
  `7defedef032f6af38bbce0165eb6c2bdec327df7`.
- Control remained exact and clean at the frozen R7 control release.
- nginx and S7 remained active.
- S8 Landing and S10 WMS failed with `S9_AGGREGATE_STATE_INVALID`; S8 Telegram
  remained inactive after fail-closed rollback.
- The five tested public Want Me Seen endpoints returned HTTP 502.
- Community processing was inactive and BotFather group joining was disabled.
- Adult media, AVS, payments, external publishing and real acquisition stayed
  closed.

## Root cause

The target release extended the anonymous shared aggregate event allowlist with
`COMMUNITY_CTA`. A real, explicitly authorized friend test created such an
aggregate. The older source release only accepts `LANDING_VIEW` and
`TELEGRAM_CTA`, so it correctly rejected the forward-shaped file. The R7 backup
and rollback covered Git, configuration, units, executables and database
evidence but not `/var/lib/tu1nz-adult-public-s9/landing-aggregates.json`.

## Recovery decision

Do not invoke the cutover or its rollback again. Do not change Application
logic and do not mutate the database. Use the separately reviewed recovery to
preserve the exact original bytes and isolate the forward-only entries, then
atomically restore the source-compatible aggregate view. On any unexpected
condition, restore the original bytes and leave affected services stopped.
